  "body": "From this elevated Big Manly position, the views are exceptional. The northern and eastern outlook takes in Manly Beach, Kawau Island and Little Barrier, while the southern views stretch towards Rangitoto. Few properties on the Hibiscus Coast capture such expansive coastal views in multiple directions. With four bedrooms, two bathrooms, a double garage and room outside for the kids, this ticks every box for a family home on the Coast.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, the open-plan kitchen, dining and lounge make the most of the outlook, with generous double glazing bringing the coastal scenery into the living areas. The renovated kitchen is beautifully presented with a central island and excellent bench space, while sliding doors extend the living onto the elevated deck. Three heat pumps provide year-round comfort throughout the home.\r\n\r\nFour bedrooms are arranged across both levels, with one upstairs and three downstairs, providing plenty of flexibility for children, guests or working from home. Two bathrooms support family living, including an upstairs bathroom with a double vanity and glass-enclosed shower.\r\n\r\nOutside, the elevated decks provide outstanding spaces to enjoy the views, while downstairs a sheltered outdoor area connects with the lawn and established greenery. There is room for children to play, a separate home gym, a double garage and additional off-street parking.\r\n\r\nSet back from the road, the property has direct access to Shuttleworth Reserve and is approximately an eight-minute walk from Big Manly Beach. Whangaparaoa Primary School, Whangaparaoa College, Edith Hopper Park, Coast Plaza, Stanmore Bay Leisure Centre and Stanmore Bay Beach are also within easy reach.\r\n\r\nBenefit from Penlink currently under construction and due for completion in 2029. The new 7km highway will strengthen the transport network support economic growth and better connect the Hibiscus Coast.\r\n\r\nBeing sold by deadline sale on 19 November, unless sold prior. \r\n\r\nContact Scott Franks to arrange a viewing.",
